  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "When Gong Wan Ting asks who will take the first battle against Xue Wu Hen, this young Gu Immortal stands and says he, Ye Lui Xiao Jin, is willing. He came to the blood battle competition under senior company, still unknown and without a name. Ye Lui Hui Hong praises that the junior is talented in fighting and often pulls brilliant moves, and that even the tribe’s first supreme elder has praised him repeatedly. Gong Wan Ting agrees to see Ye Lui tribe’s valiance. Leaving Golden Dawn Hall he gives Nian Er Ping Zhi a deep glance with golden eyes, wanting to establish his name as other young righteous path Gu Immortals refuse to feel defeated after Iron Eagle blessed land.",
      "chapters": [
        1194
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_gong_wan_ting",
        "char_xue_wu_hen",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_ye_lui_hui_hong",
        "fac_ye_lui_tribe",
        "house_golden_dawn_hall",
        "char_nian_er_ping_zhi",
        "loc_iron_eagle_blessed_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After losing to Xue Wu Hen he returns with his right arm still frozen, black and blue from the cold that reaches bones and blood. He keeps his head lowered in pain. Ye Lui Hui Hong consoles him that the loss is not his fault and that the opponent was too strong, even killing Liu Hui afterward.",
      "chapters": [
        1195
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "defeat-and-frozen-arm",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_liu_hui"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Narration calls him a genius of Ye Lui tribe who unfortunately lost to Xue Wu Hen, while Nian Er Ping Zhi killed rank seven Granny Yin, making the comparison clear to everyone.",
      "chapters": [
        1196
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "compared-with-sword-child",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_granny_yin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Young and full of vigor, he is most dissatisfied when Liu Guan Yi insults Ye Lui Qun Xing. He stands and shouts that Liu Guan Yi does not dare to show skills yet has quite the mouth, and that humiliating Lord Qun Xing is intentional fear rather than pride.",
      "chapters": [
        1202
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "insult-at-liu-guan-yi",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ye_lui_qun_xing"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He subconsciously stands in worry during Ye Lui Qun Xing’s chase, then laughs heartily at Golden Dawn Hall’s entrance, taunting Liu Guan Yi to keep boasting and yelling. Sensing the ancient sword dragon’s fury, he laughs again.",
      "chapters": [
        1204
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "taunt-at-the-hall",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
